"""ZenRay Meshes V4, level 1: the tracing of every view (10 November 2026).

The reference image itself is traced, as with tracing paper: the outline of the object to sub-pixel, every thin dark
line, every facet edge. The result is a vector drawing per view (fair lines between nodes) in the format the plan
solver reads (graph_<view>.json), an SVG, an overlay for the eye, and a check against the image.

    Trace.py build  <views_dir> <frame.json> <out_dir> [views]      graph_<view>.json, sil_<view>.png, trace_<view>.svg, overlay_<view>.png
    Trace.py check  <views_dir> <out_dir> [views]                   trace-check.json: lines found, lines true, outline distance, per view
    Trace.py board  <out_dir> <out.png>                             the six tracings on one blue sheet
    Trace.py selftest

